[brief] The focused arXiv search found one directly relevant 2024 analysis, Chen and Zhang’s study of BBN limits on heavy neutrino production and decay (arXiv:2410.07343), but no clearly relevant 2025–2026 ke
**Survey** — 29 tools on 2 servers, 5 read-only probes, 5 papers found.

The focused arXiv search found one directly relevant 2024 analysis, Chen and Zhang’s study of BBN limits on heavy neutrino production and decay (arXiv:2410.07343), but no clearly relevant 2025–2026 keV-sterile-DM-plus-BBN paper was returned. That work treats mass and active–sterile mixing as the only parameters and includes temporary matter domination, meson/photon/neutrino injection, and flavor dependence; its BBN-excluded region is complementary to laboratory HNL searches (https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.07343). For keV sterile-neutrino dark matter, BBN is generally not the dominant constraint when the particle is sufficiently long-lived: X-ray decay limits, phase-space and Lyman-alpha structure limits, and the relic-abundance mechanism usually control viability. The simplest non-resonant Dodelson–Widrow production scenario is widely regarded as excluded or highly disfavored by the combination of X-ray and small-scale-structure constraints, while viable possibilities remain in resonant production with a lepton asymmetry, mixed cold-plus-warm models, or models with additional interactions; the precise surviving bands depend strongly on the production assumptions and adopted structure-formation data.

Quantities worth checking: Sterile-neutrino mass m_s and each flavor mixing |U_es|^2, |U_mus|^2, and |U_taus|^2, or equivalently sin^2(2theta) where appropriate; Thermal production yield and relic-density fraction f_s relative to the observed dark-matter density; Sterile-neutrino radiative-decay lifetime and predicted X-ray line flux; Momentum-distribution moments, average comoving momentum, and an equivalent thermal-WDM mass; Free-streaming horizon, half-mode wavenumber, and suppression of the linear matter power spectrum; Lepton asymmetry L required for resonant Shi–Fuller production and the resulting resonance history.
