**Finding:** The 2024 Chen–Zhang minimal HNL analysis treats (m4, |Ua4|^2) as the only parameters and finds BBN exclusion only in an intermediate-mixing window: large mixing decays before BBN, while tiny mixing produces too little freeze-in abundance to affect light elements; it includes temporary matter domination and charged-meson, photon, and neutrino injection, with a separate CMB constraint for very long-lived states.
[tool] tc-261015_2-w1-d-02-32 -> ok: Recorded finding f-001.
[usage]
[tool] d-02 post_finding {"claim": "Minimal Dodelson\u2013Widrow sterile-neutrino production that supplies all dark matter is excluded by X-ray constraints in the cited self-interaction
[finding] f-002 Minimal Dodelson–Widrow sterile-neutrino production that supplies all dark matter is excluded by X-ray constraints in the cited self-interaction study, while no
**Finding:** Minimal Dodelson–Widrow sterile-neutrino production that supplies all dark matter is excluded by X-ray constraints in the cited self-interaction study, while nonstandard active-neutrino self-interactions can widen or shift the correct-abundance region toward smaller or larger mixing; allowing a subdominant 'cocktail' fraction further relaxes X-ray limits, and the study reports no structure-formation problem from the extra interactions in its benchmark framework.
[tool] tc-261015_2-w1-d-02-33 -> ok: Recorded finding f-002.
[usage]
[tool] d-02 post_finding {"claim": "Resonant Shi\u2013Fuller production requires an initial neutrino lepton number many orders of magnitude above the baryon-to-photon ratio but below de
[finding] f-003 Resonant Shi–Fuller production requires an initial neutrino lepton number many orders of magnitude above the baryon-to-photon ratio but below detectable CMB/BBN
**Finding:** Resonant Shi–Fuller production requires an initial neutrino lepton number many orders of magnitude above the baryon-to-photon ratio but below detectable CMB/BBN limits in the 7.1-keV mixed cold-plus-warm study; the paper computes the distribution by Boltzmann evolution including the density potential proportional to lepton asymmetry and assesses viability through satellite-host subhalo formation rather than a full BBN abundance fit.
[tool] tc-261015_2-w1-d-02-34 -> ok: Recorded finding f-003.
[usage]
[tool] d-02 post_finding {"claim": "The scalar-mediated freeze-in/freeze-out benchmark produces keV sterile dark matter through a two-step process: Higgs-portal freeze-in of a complex s
[finding] f-004 The scalar-mediated freeze-in/freeze-out benchmark produces keV sterile dark matter through a two-step process: Higgs-portal freeze-in of a complex scalar secto
**Finding:** The scalar-mediated freeze-in/freeze-out benchmark produces keV sterile dark matter through a two-step process: Higgs-portal freeze-in of a complex scalar sector followed by sterile-neutrino production from scalar decays and annihilations; the hidden sector can thermalize at a temperature below the SM temperature, changing the momentum distribution and free-streaming relative to oscillation production.
[tool] tc-261015_2-w1-d-02-35 -> ok: Recorded finding f-004.
