**Completed — Survey 2024–2026 arXiv literature directly addressing sterile-neutrino dark matter, BBN constraints, and the surviving mass–mixing parameter regions..** (Tool budget was exhausted before full-text chunk reading, figure extraction, and exact contour/citation validation.) Survey established several relevant 2024–2025 papers. The directly relevant minimal HNL-BBN analysis arXiv:2410.07343 uses (m4, |U_a4|^2) separately for a=e, μ, τ and includes temporary matter domination plus meson, photon, and neutrino injection; full text saved at /Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/hep-testing-research/runs/261015_205132/2410.07343.txt. arXiv:2507.12270 reports tau_N < approximately 0.02 s for thermally equilibrated HNLs and finds dark decays generally strengthen BBN and Delta N_eff constraints; text saved at .../2507.12270.txt. The nonminimal ALP cascade model arXiv:2410.06970 opens an approximately 1 MeV–1 GeV and 10^-9–10^-6 mixing-strength region, subject to later ALP cosmological constraints; text saved at .../2410.06970.txt. The resonant keV-DM analysis arXiv:2510.01907 finds regions consistent with X-ray and Lyman-alpha constraints for lepton-to-entropy ratio at least order 10^-3 and m_s approximately above 20 keV; production during lepton-number injection can reduce the required mixing and free-streaming length; text saved at .../2510.01907.txt. The 2024 Affleck–Dine/L-ball study arXiv:2402.11902 addresses resonant Shi–Fuller production and X-ray/Lyman-alpha constraints but its abstract gives no numerical mass–mixing interval and is not a direct BBN analysis. No figures or captions were extracted. Full-text chunk reading, validated verbatim citations, exact exclusion contours, explicit mixing intervals for arXiv:2410.07343, and quantitative electron/muon/tau contour values remain open. The autonomous survey failed with a Search.results runtime error, although four direct full-text downloads succeeded.
